# No removed normals API (pre-4.1 auto smooth)

Blender 4.1 removed auto smooth as a mesh setting and made normals always
current. The old calls are among the most common errors in generated
Blender code, because nearly every pre-4.1 import, cleanup and export
script used them. On 4.5 LTS and 5.x each one raises:

```text
AttributeError: 'Mesh' object has no attribute 'use_auto_smooth'
```

Measured on 4.5.14 and 5.2.1: none of `use_auto_smooth`,
`auto_smooth_angle`, `calc_normals_split`, `free_normals_split` and
`create_normals_split` exists on `bpy.types.Mesh`.

## What this rule flags

- `.use_auto_smooth` (read or assignment)
- `.auto_smooth_angle`
- `.calc_normals_split(`, `.free_normals_split(`, `.create_normals_split(`
- Reading `loop.normal` after a `calc_normals_split()` call, a pattern whose
  first line already fails

## Wrong

```python
import math
import bpy

me = obj.data
me.use_auto_smooth = True
me.auto_smooth_angle = math.radians(30)
me.calc_normals_split()
normals = [loop.normal.copy() for loop in me.loops]
me.free_normals_split()
```

## Right

```python
import math
import bpy

me = obj.data
# Destructive auto smooth: marks edges sharper than the angle as sharp
# AND sets every face smooth (a flat mesh comes out smooth-shaded).
me.set_sharp_from_angle(angle=math.radians(30))
# Always current; no calc call, nothing to free.
normals = [n.vector.copy() for n in me.corner_normals]
```

For a non-destructive equivalent, `bpy.ops.object.shade_auto_smooth(angle=...)`
adds a "Smooth by Angle" geometry-nodes modifier (measured on 5.2.1). Under
`--background --factory-startup` on 4.5.14 it returned `{'CANCELLED'}` and
added nothing, so headless scripts that must also run on 4.5 should use
`set_sharp_from_angle`.

| Removed | Replacement |
| --- | --- |
| `mesh.use_auto_smooth = True` + `auto_smooth_angle` | `mesh.set_sharp_from_angle(angle=...)`, or the `shade_auto_smooth` operator |
| `mesh.calc_normals_split()` then `loop.normal` | `mesh.corner_normals[i].vector` |
| `mesh.free_normals_split()` | nothing: delete the call |
| `mesh.create_normals_split()` | nothing; custom normals via `mesh.normals_split_custom_set(...)` |
| face/vertex normal reads | `mesh.polygon_normals`, `mesh.vertex_normals` |

`mesh.normals_domain` (`'POINT'`, `'FACE'` or `'CORNER'`) says which domain
the normals actually vary on. Read it instead of tracking an auto-smooth
flag.

## Verified

[`examples/mesh-normals-after-41/`](../examples/mesh-normals-after-41/), on
4.5.14 and 5.2.1:

- The pre-4.1 code raises `AttributeError`.
- `set_sharp_from_angle(30°)` on a flat 16-sided cylinder marks the 32
  cap-rim edges and smooths all 18 faces.
- A rim vertex has two corner normals, and three once the faces are
  flattened again, with no recompute call.

Copy-paste replacement: [`snippets/set-sharp-from-angle.py`](../snippets/set-sharp-from-angle.py).

